            <ArticleTitle>Targeted tumor detection: guidelines for developing biotinylated diagnostics.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2154-2157</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc00311k</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The challenge in achieving precision medicine relies on how to advance and/or enhance new as well as old therapeutic strategies. Here, we highlight the significant role hydrophilicity of biotinylated fluorescent probe's plays on their cellular uptake behaviour.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
